{"id": "EUVD-2026-71289", "enisaUuid": "5e3707ae-58df-363a-9b3a-d1681f5396f6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: reject unrepresentable multicast TVLV offsets\n\nThe network and transport header fields in struct sk_buff are 16-bit\noffsets from skb->head, and U16_MAX is reserved as the unset transport\nheader value. batadv_tvlv_call_handler() sets both fields from a received\nmulticast TVLV without checking whether the TVLV end is representable.\n\nIf the end offset exceeds the field's range, skb_set_transport_header()\ntruncates it so that the transport header precedes the network header.\nThe negative difference is then returned by skb_network_header_len() as\na large u32. batadv_mcast_forw_packet() consequently accepts an oversized\nmulticast tracker and accesses memory beyond the skb data.\n\nAdd skb_set_transport_header_careful(), an offset-aware counterpart to\nskb_reset_transport_header_careful(), which validates the final\nhead-relative offset before assigning it. Use the new helper in\nbatadv_tvlv_call_handler() and reject unrepresentable TVLVs before\nsetting the network header.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da1f5aa7ec93f2cc17f5cd30efc54f62af433cf2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/916ec741e65af072b98e475feaad98c063da1b7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b466746fe109127fd983100a228cdd1f1f6ece2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b46baa591d0a7c16b62f150917187e70d053be6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f12c2de4f542e3220e17e0606f492110064f04cb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80839", "GHSA-676r-cqgf-36vf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2511a689-8469-3ea3-8f73-ef57d669a601", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "3263a7e5-7342-3d94-a7ac-e965cb704ba0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3c16e52b-34ff-3b5d-97a2-2cf471d0e68f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07afe1ba288c04280622fa002ed385f1ac0b6fe6 <1b466746fe109127fd983100a228cdd1f1f6ece2"}, {"id": "7372bc80-825f-39c1-baf6-c4a3d339d1bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07afe1ba288c04280622fa002ed385f1ac0b6fe6 <2b46baa591d0a7c16b62f150917187e70d053be6"}, {"id": "7cbea96f-4c1b-3679-aa39-b3005c33b5f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07afe1ba288c04280622fa002ed385f1ac0b6fe6 <da1f5aa7ec93f2cc17f5cd30efc54f62af433cf2"}, {"id": "7cf985f2-12ee-30fe-a9e1-6d1772700580", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "96d98584-c63b-300f-837b-84b323b91531", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ada13743-cb0e-34c0-9a22-1afd3a6cdc9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07afe1ba288c04280622fa002ed385f1ac0b6fe6 <916ec741e65af072b98e475feaad98c063da1b7c"}, {"id": "b040b8f6-6fdd-36e1-9343-72c50106b8c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "b53a45f6-a5fa-3ea8-a31a-349fd11279e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.108"}, {"id": "b97a2e11-c0c2-3dc9-b841-2c031efa1830", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.13"}, {"id": "f315f047-aaf1-3629-a88f-897fe8bd2274", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07afe1ba288c04280622fa002ed385f1ac0b6fe6 <f12c2de4f542e3220e17e0606f492110064f04cb"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "71ee51e4-3423-33fc-bf35-95b0b085ec8e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}